<div class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Security and privacy</p>
  <h1>Built to be trusted with people’s details</h1>
  <p class="lede">Care Core holds information about staff and about people who receive care. This is a plain summary of how it is protected, and where the responsibility passes to you.</p>
</div>
<div class="cols3">
  <div><h2>Access by role</h2><p>Administrator, manager and staff roles are enforced on the server for every page and action. Care information is for managers and administrators only. One organisation can never see another’s records.</p></div>
  <div><h2>Encrypted where it matters</h2><p>National Insurance and bank details are encrypted in the database (AES-256-GCM). Passwords are stored only as hashes; invitations and integration tokens only as hashes, shown once.</p></div>
  <div><h2>A second pair of eyes</h2><p>When staff ask to change their name, address, National Insurance, bank details, photo or signature, their line manager or HR approves it first. Nobody can approve their own request.</p></div>
  <div><h2>Access that ends on time</h2><p>A leaver’s login stops after their last day because every request is checked against that date. It does not depend on an overnight job.</p></div>
  <div><h2>A complete audit trail</h2><p>Every change is recorded with who made it, in the same transaction as the change. Sensitive values are never written to the log or to outgoing events.</p></div>
  <div><h2>Safe sign-in</h2><p>Microsoft sign-in with full token checks, rate-limited password sign-in, private session cookies, and protection against forged forms and injected scripts.</p></div>
</div>
<section class="prose" style="max-width:52rem">
  <h2>What we do not claim</h2>
  <p>Care Core is a tool, not a certificate. You remain the data controller. Lawful basis, privacy notices, retention periods, subject access requests, backups, server patching and a security review before real data goes in are your organisation’s responsibility. Multi-factor authentication for password sign-in, automated retention and a subject-access export are not built yet (Microsoft sign-in lets you apply your tenant’s multi-factor rules).</p>
  <p><a href="/docs/security">Read the full security and privacy page</a> · <a href="/docs/limits">What it does not do yet</a> · <a href="/docs/faq">Questions and answers</a></p>
</section>
